{"id":15694,"ord":56,"n_segments":59,"prev":15693,"next":15695,"doc":{"id":"mr-ernest--punch--miller-1959-09-25","title":"Ernest 'Punch' Miller Interview, 1959-09-25","collection":"tulane","inst":"Tulane — Hogan Jazz Archive","interviewee":"Ernest 'Punch' Miller","interviewer":"Richard B. 'Dick' Allen","date":"1959-09-25","year":1959,"source_url":"https://musicrising.tulane.edu/listen/interviews/ernest-punch-miller-1959-09-25/","url":"https://semlab.io/linked-jazz-transcripts/?t=mr-ernest--punch--miller-1959-09-25"},"chapter":"New Orleans trombonists, drummers, pianists","title":"Trombonists in early New Orleans","category":"music_technique_style","summary":"Punch names early trombonists.","period":"c. 1915","year_from":1915,"year_to":1915,"words":91,"start":[6,38],"end":[6,43],"url":"https://semlab.io/linked-jazz-transcripts/?t=mr-ernest--punch--miller-1959-09-25#s15694","tags":{"places":[],"venues":[],"bands":[{"name":"Buddy Petit's band","focus":0,"leader":"Buddy Petit"}]},"people":[{"name":"George Washington","qid":null,"n":2},{"name":"Buddy Petit","qid":"Q1001073","n":1},{"name":"Kid Rena","qid":"Q1150630","n":1},{"name":"Morris French","qid":null,"n":1},{"name":"Earl Humphrey","qid":"Q5325923","n":1},{"name":"Kid Ory","qid":"Q441399","n":1},{"name":"Jack Carey","qid":"Q6111565","n":1},{"name":"Willie Humphrey","qid":"Q2330233","n":1}],"story":{"theme":25,"theme_name":"Trombonists: who they heard, admired and learned from","community":50,"community_name":"Talking trombonists: who played the slide and how","core":true},"blocks":[{"p":6,"b":38,"s":"Richard B. 'Dick' Allen","x":"Who were some of the good trombone players down here when you were young?"},{"p":6,"b":39,"s":"Ernest 'Punch' Miller","x":"Morris French, Kid Ory, Jack Keran, and let's see who else I can... Who was with Buddy Petit? Morris French was with Rene. I'm trying to... Oh, yeah, a little boy, George Washington. He never did come back. Little bit of fella. Played nice trombone."},{"p":6,"b":40,"s":"Richard B. 'Dick' Allen","x":"What happened to him?"},{"p":6,"b":41,"s":"Ernest 'Punch' Miller","x":"And they had another bad man, Willie Umford's brother, Earl Umford. He was bad."},{"p":6,"b":42,"s":"Richard B. 'Dick' Allen","x":"What happened to George Washington?"},{"p":6,"b":43,"s":"Ernest 'Punch' Miller","x":"I don't know. That family ain't ever come back."}]}